WEBVTT

1
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:22.510
For those of you
following along in TWS,

2
00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:24.550
this video aims to show you how

3
00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:27.325
to add common contracts
to the display.

4
00:00:27.325 --> 00:00:29.590
We will explain contract codes

5
00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:32.200
and months to help you
quickly build them.

6
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.870
We'll demonstrate how to add one,

7
00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.195
or a strip of futures
contracts to your display.

8
00:00:38.195 --> 00:00:41.010
For spread traders, and
for those wanting to roll

9
00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.615
a contract from one
exploration to the next,

10
00:00:43.615 --> 00:00:44.890
we'll show you how to create

11
00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:47.300
a spread between two contract.

12
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.940
In TWS, future symbols are

13
00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:52.639
specific to the exchange
listed contract,

14
00:00:52.639 --> 00:00:55.955
month, and year of the
product you are looking at.

15
00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.560
Yet, there are several ways to

16
00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:00.080
arrive at displaying
the information.

17
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.790
If you know the symbol of

18
00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:04.100
the contract you want
to add to the display,

19
00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.800
type it into a row
on your monitor.

20
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.340
In this case, I'll
use GC for gold.

21
00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:15.100
By entering GC, the contract
selection box displays.

22
00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:18.875
Locate the exchange in
which this contract trades,

23
00:01:18.875 --> 00:01:22.400
select "Futures", and
pick the relevant month.

24
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.280
If the month you want
is not displayed,

25
00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:28.975
click the "More" button to
find the relevant contract.

26
00:01:28.975 --> 00:01:32.420
You will notice that there
are a few nearby contracts

27
00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:36.395
listed along with the
so-called continuous contract.

28
00:01:36.395 --> 00:01:38.990
The continuous contract refers to

29
00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:41.630
the contract where most
investors are positioned,

30
00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:44.525
and where open interest
is concentrated.

31
00:01:44.525 --> 00:01:46.820
TWS will update as

32
00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:49.795
positions are rolled
into the next expiry.

33
00:01:49.795 --> 00:01:52.399
To quickly add a
specific exploration

34
00:01:52.399 --> 00:01:54.500
for a contract in to TWs,

35
00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:55.985
you will need the product code,

36
00:01:55.985 --> 00:01:58.220
and the symbol used
to denote the month,

37
00:01:58.220 --> 00:01:59.810
along with the final digits of

38
00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:02.104
the year in which the
contract expires.

39
00:02:02.104 --> 00:02:05.030
For example, if I specifically
wanted to display

40
00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:08.015
the December 2021 contract,

41
00:02:08.015 --> 00:02:11.360
we know that GC is the
TWS symbol for gold,

42
00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:14.450
and knowing that Z
represents December,

43
00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:17.305
we'd enter GC Z 1,

44
00:02:17.305 --> 00:02:20.615
where one represents 2021.

45
00:02:20.615 --> 00:02:23.915
Should you want the
December 2022 contract,

46
00:02:23.915 --> 00:02:27.720
you'd enter GC Z 2.

47
00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:32.365
Here is a list of the
futures month codes.

48
00:02:32.365 --> 00:02:36.260
To display multiple contract
months at the same time,

49
00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:38.165
start with the TWS symbol,

50
00:02:38.165 --> 00:02:41.500
locate the exchange,
and select futures.

51
00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:45.180
Select "More", and hold
the "Control" key down as

52
00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.710
you highlight the expirations

53
00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:49.260
you wish to add to your display.

54
00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:52.620
This is known as a future strip.

55
00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.350
You can add all of

56
00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:55.910
your required futures contracts

57
00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:58.045
to a monitor page this way.

58
00:02:58.045 --> 00:03:00.405
To learn more about
each contract,

59
00:03:00.405 --> 00:03:03.020
or to find out it's
trading hours and so on,

60
00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:04.280
right-click on the symbol,

61
00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:07.040
and from the financial
instrument info row,

62
00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:10.100
follow the arrow to
view its description.

63
00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.600
You will be able to see

64
00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.225
the exchange
information, contract,

65
00:03:14.225 --> 00:03:17.765
expiration, and last
trading details,

66
00:03:17.765 --> 00:03:20.135
as well as trading hours.

67
00:03:20.135 --> 00:03:22.940
Click-through the calendar
hyperlink to get a

68
00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:26.110
visual on trading
hours across the week.

69
00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:29.585
To display futures related
data on your monitor,

70
00:03:29.585 --> 00:03:31.355
right-click on any column header,

71
00:03:31.355 --> 00:03:33.395
and choose "Manage Columns"

72
00:03:33.395 --> 00:03:35.910
to display the
configuration menu.

73
00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:39.250
From the available columns
to the right of the display,

74
00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:41.830
locate, and expand
the futures grouping,

75
00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:43.840
and make your selections.

76
00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:45.985
Note that you should choose

77
00:03:45.985 --> 00:03:47.620
other common values from

78
00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.630
financial instrument
descriptions,

79
00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:52.255
prices, and high, low,

80
00:03:52.255 --> 00:03:55.690
volume, history,
sections as usual.

81
00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:59.035
If you wish to add a spread
between two contracts,

82
00:03:59.035 --> 00:04:00.370
you can use the convention of

83
00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:02.885
subtracting one
contract from another.

84
00:04:02.885 --> 00:04:05.710
For example, for gold contracts,

85
00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:09.100
to add the spread between
the December 2021,

86
00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.115
and June 2022 explorations,

87
00:04:12.115 --> 00:04:19.800
type GC Z 1 minus GC
M 2, and hit "Enter".

88
00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:22.460
You will see the bid ask prices,

89
00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:25.735
and the chart display the
recent history of the spread.

90
00:04:25.735 --> 00:04:30.420
Alternatively, enter GC in
the monitor, locate futures,

91
00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:33.129
and select
"Combinations", "Smart",

92
00:04:33.129 --> 00:04:35.120
and from the combo selection tool

93
00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.385
build the correct strategy.

94
00:04:37.385 --> 00:04:40.520
There is a lot of
information in this video to

95
00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:42.920
help you locate futures
contract details,

96
00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:47.130
and symbols, and how to add
them to your monitor page.